id: pm-evidence-backend-conformance
title: Verify backend-aware SDK atomic evidence mutations when supported
description: The pinned SDK commitItemMutations API accepts a filesystem tracker root and cannot inject a remote mutation client. Keep remote backend mutation conformance explicitly unclaimed until the SDK exposes equivalent lock-held expected-state writes through the active backend. No hosted services were accessed.
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: "gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1399",sdk-gap,"upstream:pm-cli#1399"
created_at: "2026-10-23T07:47:59.020Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T05:46:26.454Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Backend-aware SDK transaction API available; run concurrent distinct and duplicate review conformance against supported backends before claiming support
parent: pm-evidence-build
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T05:39:39.135Z",codex-agent,"Criterion adapter scope audit: installed public declarations expose commitItemMutations(options: CommitItemMutationsOptions) with required pmRoot and no backend client; getItemAt(id,target,{pmRoot,cwd}) and readHistoryEntries(path,id) likewise provide local history transport. Runtime PmClient has no backend history-read method. Open upstream backend-neutral capability plan is unbraind/pm-cli#1399 (search: history backend). Criterion generation identity therefore shares this existing local-history/transaction limitation; remote backend conformance remains unclaimed, and no hosted data was accessed."
body: ""
